 <a id="terminal-command"></a>
 
+## Browser pane DevTools access
+
+The product document can send an allowed set of Chrome DevTools Protocol commands to a Browser pane page it holds a lease for (`dshDesktop.browserDevtools(guestId, method, params)`, Harness Studio patch): real input (`Input.dispatchMouseEvent`, `Input.dispatchKeyEvent`, `Input.insertText`, `Input.dispatchScrollEvent`), `Page.captureScreenshot`, `Page.getLayoutMetrics`, `Page.reload`, `Runtime.evaluate`, DOM reads, `Accessibility.getFullAXTree` and `Network.getResponseBody`. The pseudo-method `Harness.events` with `{ since, kinds? }` returns the page's buffered console messages, uncaught exceptions with stack frames, log entries and network requests, responses and failures, in sequence order, as `{ events, latest, dropped: { console, network } }`. Each kind has its own ring (console, exception and log keep the latest 300 each; request, response and failed the latest 500 each), so heavy network traffic cannot push errors out; `dropped` counts what each group's rings have evicted, and `kinds` limits the reply to the kinds named. The main process attaches the debugger on the first command, enables the Runtime, Log, Network and Page domains, refuses any other method and any page outside the sender's own leases, and forgets the buffer when the page closes. Only pages on this computer or the local network (loopback, `0.0.0.0`, `.localhost`, `.test` and `.local` names, private addresses) are read: commands for other pages are refused, the debugger detaches when a page starts loading, is redirected to, or commits another address, and a command that lands mid-navigation re-checks the address after attaching. Navigation stays with the pane and its main-process checks. Source: [`src/browser-devtools.ts`](src/browser-devtools.ts).
+
 ## Terminal command
 
 The application menu's **Install Command-Line Tool…** entry, immediately below **Check for Updates…**, shows the current command and offers Install, Repair, and Remove. The `harness-studio` command uses Desktop's installed runtime and the ordinary [dsh CLI](../cli/README.md), including when the Desktop application is closed. Open a new terminal after installation and run `harness-studio --version`.
